by lazerg at 2026-11-06T15:35:45Z

When the TraceableResponse is freed normally (refcount or GC), properties are released in declaration order, so that part doesn't depend on object ids. It does at shutdown though: for objects still alive then, PHP calls destructors in object id order, and since ids get reused the canary can end up first, so the event would stop a bit early there. The response stays usable either way, which is the actual fix, so I didn't think the timing at shutdown was worth more code, but let me know if you see it differently.

